calling the coupled repository generator. After 15/15 reproducibility and all
four native rows pass, one coordinated staged boundary rotates the accepted
asset contract, supply-chain source, validator version and exact accepted
archive task/resource/SHA constants, both default archive paths, Swift
acceptance assertions, generated inventory/provenance/notices/catalog, and the
trusted five-file bundle. The generator never sees mutually inconsistent old
and new contracts.

The runbook identifies and enforces the exact ten tracked files for an ordinary
source/version/archive rotation. It requires an isolated no-local/no-hardlink
clone, a new task-board archive outcome, exact archive retrieval/comparison,
generation/audit/tests/bundle checks in the clone, a reviewed binary patch,
clean accepted-tree guards before patching, and identical regenerated outputs
after patching. Toolchain, license, protocol/schema, runtime-policy, ownership,
or generator changes must extend the exact allowlist/tests; operators may not
