--
1318-- FIX: Every runtime subprocess now executes inside a verified fail-closed boundary: macOS sandbox rules deny file writes, networking, and process forks; Linux Landlock denies filesystem mutation and seccomp denies sockets and non-thread process creation. A live probe must prove all three denials before identity execution. Reports use bounded fixed-vocabulary commands and validated runner metadata, and every subprocess check records whether a process started plus any observed exit code.
1319-- VERIFICATION: Real detached-descendant and external-write fixtures fail before residue can escape, leave no marker or process, and preserve the nonzero exit. Native and emulated private-path/oversized-metadata fixtures remain path-free and bounded. The expanded 16-test suite passes with `ResourceWarning` promoted to errors; full regression and native asset evidence are recorded in the task outcome.
1320-
1321-### 1655 — Relay SPDX metadata is reproducible across clean workspaces (TASK-260715-1q03sa)
1322:- FINDING: Existing double-build executable and protocol-test bytes were identical, but Syft 1.48.0 emitted a wall-clock `creationInfo.created` value and random UUID suffix in `documentNamespace` for each SPDX file. Those eight metadata differences cascaded into different four-entry manifest and checksum bytes, while the comparator checked only executables and incorrectly passed.
1323-- FIX: SPDX output now derives its UTC creation time from the required `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`, derives its path-free namespace from the exact executable name and SHA-256, and serializes recursively sorted JSON. The reproducibility comparator now requires the exact 11-file release tree and four protocol-test binaries, compares modes and SHA-256, and reports bounded semantic JSON paths plus the first raw byte offset on drift.
1324:- VERIFICATION: Two isolated clean-cache clones of source commit `e8bd954a1985e0a3204504209f1b022f71e4d1f9`, relay tree `4f52531c3a84bd059fb5be4893f4ed22115cb818`, recipe SHA-256 `10051c52c85e7a43d03362aa8ee4dbe1b6954410c258c801b7e1dd483532b2de`, Go 1.26.5, Syft 1.48.0, and epoch `1787158980` matched 15/15 outputs byte-for-byte. Their normalized four-member archive also matched at SHA-256 `09014b22e694b1ff4ab664c81d46b3afccd5a973f701cbd4625bfd88c093ab40`. The manifest SHA-256 is `ef5bd8b3cc41ce0e30c026bd088b370faeea30d789a7c6708631330afe8b049d`; a copied Linux/amd64 one-byte mutation deterministically produced `ba7db4548bd3c974bf6651fc4e9686a4267d2874c74123df6c5af6a09da89579` twice without changing canonical bytes.
1325-- SAFETY: The proof was offline and rootless. It did not sign, notarize, install, launch an app/provider, start a VPN, or mutate routes, interfaces, packet filters, or DNS.
1326-
1327:### 1905 — Relay asset runbook preserves split historical pins (TASK-260715-u8tkx0)
1328-- FINDING: The accepted archive binds relay source commit `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096` to byte-affecting recipe commit `4326036a26a515d5d349e669574323d4d1c7259c`; overlaying the three pinned recipe files makes the historical source checkout intentionally dirty, so a truthful rebuild verifies compiled source separately and uses tool provenance rather than claiming `--require-clean`.
1329-- ANOMALY: The historical recipe predates the safe `archive-assets` subcommand. The operator procedure uses the current non-byte-affecting, ownership-safe archive writer only after both four-target builds, then makes the retained archive comparison authoritative instead of presenting the missing historical command as runnable.
1330-- VERIFICATION: Two independent no-local/no-hardlink clones rebuilt all four accepted executables and normalized archives. Both archives were byte-identical to each other and to the retained `TASK-260715-24icoz` archive at SHA-256 `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`; trusted bundle generation/check passed and its manifest was byte-identical to the current bundled manifest. No signing, installation, application/provider launch, VPN, route, interface, packet-filter, DNS, or remote execution occurred.
1331:- REVIEW ANOMALY: A fresh reviewer proved that the historical full-tree command could not reproduce raw Syft 1.48.0 metadata: random `documentNamespace` UUIDs and wall-clock `creationInfo.created` values changed all four SPDX files and cascaded into the release-builder manifest/checksums. The documented direct cross-clone comparator also violated its `.build/relay` path-containment contract.
1332-- RESOLUTION: The runbook now limits the historical claim to the exact executables/archive and deterministically regenerated trusted application manifest, requires immutable retention for old release-builder metadata, and routes every new candidate through the accepted `TASK-260715-1q03sa` normalization recipe. Both clone outputs are staged below one invoked checkout's `.build/relay` root before the exact 11-release-file plus four-protocol-test comparison. It separately identifies `relux-relay-manifest-v1.json` as unbundled release-builder/native-smoke evidence and `relux-relay-assets-v1.json` as the generated application-bundle/rollback manifest.
1333-- REWORK VERIFICATION: Fresh task-scoped clones reproduced the historical archive and all four documented executable hashes, then reproduced the deterministic reference release tree with `relay reproducibility: identical=15/15`, archive SHA-256 `09014b22e694b1ff4ab664c81d46b3afccd5a973f701cbd4625bfd88c093ab40`, and release-builder manifest SHA-256 `ef5bd8b3cc41ce0e30c026bd088b370faeea30d789a7c6708631330afe8b049d`. Two trusted application bundle generations matched as exact five-file trees; Darwin arm64 native smoke passed 17/17; copied size drift exited `2`; and a native Linux/amd64 request on Darwin/arm64 exited `1` before process start. All evidence remained build-only and credential-free.
1334-- UPDATE-ORDER ANOMALY: Rework 02 confirmed that the original step 6 could not run `relay-supply-chain-generate` for a changed source/version/archive while step 9 still retained the old asset contract. `validate_config()` requires the supply-chain source revision/version and accepted archive task/resource/SHA to equal `asset-bundle-source-v1.json`, and generation then rewrites that contract's supply-chain link and the Swift catalog. The Swift acceptance test also pins the accepted archive and build identity.
1335-- COORDINATED RESOLUTION: Candidate release-builder notices, deterministic SPDX, provenance, 15/15 reproducibility, normalized archive, and four native rows now precede repository mutation. One isolated staged boundary then rotates the two source contracts, validator constants, Makefile and asset-tool archive defaults, Swift acceptance assertions, and generated inventory/provenance/notices/catalog/bundle as an exact ten-file tracked patch. A deliberately changed `0.0.0` / `e8bd954a…` candidate proved generation, audit, 21 supply-chain tests, 26 asset-manifest tests, four Swift catalog tests, and bundle checking without changing the accepted source tree; the initial red Swift run exposed and added the missing assertion surface rather than bypassing it.

